--- !u!114 &1808463679
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1808463677}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e0a35f221ed92524c93e182a1633f0db, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: PrimalFrontier.Runtime::PrimalFrontier.Story.JournalSystem
  entries:
  - id: wreck
    title: The Wreck
    category: 0
    text: The storm broke our ship on the reef. I found no one else. The hold is
      split open and the sea has taken almost everything. What is left, I must use
      well.
    sketch: wreck
    trigger: 17
    triggerId: ZONE_Shipwreck
  - id: fresh_water
    title: Fresh Water
    category: 0
    text: A stream runs down from the hills into a quiet pond. The water is cold
      and sweet. I must stay close to it, and carry some when I can.
    sketch: water
    trigger: 12
    triggerId: fresh_water
  - id: salt_water
    title: The Sea Is Not Water
    category: 0
    text: I drank from the sea like a fool. The salt burned and the thirst came back
      worse. Only fresh water will keep me alive.
    sketch: water
    trigger: 14
    triggerId: 
  - id: fire
    title: Fire
    category: 0
    text: Fire. Warmth, light, cooked food, and a mark of safety in the dark. Rain
      eats the fuel quickly; keep wood close.
    sketch: fire
    trigger: 21
    triggerId: 
  - id: cooking
    title: Cooked Food
    category: 0
    text: Meat cooked over the coals fills me more and sits better. Raw meat is a
      gamble with my stomach.
    sketch: meat
    trigger: 23
    triggerId: 
  - id: night
    title: The First Night
    category: 0
    text: Darkness falls fast here. The air turns cold, and the forest is full of
      sounds I cannot name. Stay near the fire.
    sketch: night
    trigger: 26
    triggerId: 
  - id: shelter
    title: Shelter
    category: 0
    text: Branches and leaves, lashed together. Not much, but it keeps off the rain
      and lets me rest.
    sketch: shelter
    trigger: 20
    triggerId: shelter
  - id: stone_tools
    title: Stone Tools
    category: 2
    text: 'Strike stone on stone until an edge appears, then bind it to a haft with
      cord. My grandfather''s stories were true: a sharp stone is a second hand.'
    sketch: axe
    trigger: 8
    triggerId: stone_axe
  - id: cordage
    title: Cordage
    category: 2
    text: Plant fibre, twisted and doubled back on itself, becomes cord. Cord holds
      everything together.
    sketch: rope
    trigger: 8
    triggerId: rope
  - id: spear
    title: The Spear
    category: 2
    text: A long shaft and a knapped point. Thrust to keep distance, or throw it
      if I must. Always pick it up again.
    sketch: spear
    trigger: 8
    triggerId: stone_spear
  - id: bow
    title: Bow and Arrows
    category: 2
    text: A springy stave and a cord. Draw fully before letting go, or the arrow
      flies weak.
    sketch: bow
    trigger: 8
    triggerId: bow
  - id: beach
    title: The Beach
    category: 3
    text: White sand, driftwood, and the wreck. Behind the beach the forest rises
      towards dark hills.
    sketch: beach
    trigger: 17
    triggerId: ZONE_StartBeach
  - id: pond
    title: The Pond
    category: 3
    text: A still pond in a hollow of the forest, fed by the stream. Animals come
      here to drink. I am not the only one who knows this place.
    sketch: water
    trigger: 17
    triggerId: ZONE_Pond
  - id: meadow
    title: The Meadow
    category: 3
    text: An open meadow in the middle of the island. The grass is flattened in wide
      paths, as if something huge walks here every day.
    sketch: meadow
    trigger: 17
    triggerId: ZONE_Meadow
  - id: cave
    title: The Cave
    category: 3
    text: A cave mouth in the cliffs. Cold air breathes out of it. Shelter from rain,
      but I do not know what else sleeps inside.
    sketch: cave
    trigger: 17
    triggerId: ZONE_Cave
  - id: rocky
    title: The Rocky Hills
    category: 3
    text: Broken stone and cliffs. Good rock for tools. From up here the island looks
      bigger than I thought.
    sketch: rocks
    trigger: 17
    triggerId: ZONE_Rocky
  - id: footprint
    title: Giant Footprints
    category: 3
    text: Three toes, each longer than my forearm, pressed deep into the mud. Whatever
      made these weighs more than any ox. The tracks are fresh.
    sketch: footprint
    trigger: 19
    triggerId: 
  - id: captains_log
    title: Captain's Log
    category: 3
    text: 'Water-stained pages from the captain''s chest: ''Day 41. Compass spinning.
      Charts useless. The men speak of an island that is not on any map. Storm rising
      from the south.'' The rest is unreadable.'
    sketch: log
    trigger: 18
    triggerId: captains_log
  - id: triceratops
    title: Three-Horned Grazer
    category: 1
    text: A beast the size of a hut, with three horns and a great bony frill. It
      grazes calmly and watches me with one eye. I think it will leave me alone if
      I leave it alone.
    sketch: trike
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: triceratops
  - id: parasaurolophus
    title: Crested Callers
    category: 1
    text: They move in small groups and call to each other with long, hollow notes
      through the crests on their heads. At the first sign of danger they run.
    sketch: trike
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: parasaurolophus
  - id: ankylosaurus
    title: Armoured Tank
    category: 1
    text: Low, wide and covered in bony plates, with a heavy club at the end of its
      tail. Slow, but I would not want to stand behind it.
    sketch: rocks
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: ankylosaurus
  - id: velociraptor
    title: Small Hunters
    category: 1
    text: No taller than my waist, feathered, fast, and never alone. A hooked claw
      on each foot. They watch before they strike.
    sketch: claw
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: velociraptor
  - id: carnotaurus
    title: Horned Runner
    category: 1
    text: A tall hunter with two short horns above its eyes and tiny arms. It guards
      its ground and runs like the wind. Stay out of its sight.
    sketch: claw
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: carnotaurus
  - id: spinosaurus
    title: Sail-Back
    category: 1
    text: A long-snouted giant with a great sail on its back, hunting along the stream.
      The water is its territory.
    sketch: water
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: spinosaurus
  - id: apex
    title: The Rift Tyrant
    category: 1
    text: I heard it long before I saw it. A head as long as a man, jaws full of
      teeth like knives. Everything on this island fears it. Everything.
    sketch: claw
    trigger: 30
    triggerId: apex
  - id: predator_sign
    title: Something Hunts Here
    category: 1
    text: A roar rolled across the hills and the forest went silent. The grazers
      lifted their heads. Something on this island hunts, and it is not me.
    sketch: claw
    trigger: 31
    triggerId: 
  - id: fruit
    title: Fruit in the Crowns
    category: 0
    text: Some of the tall fern-palms carry orange fruit right under the leaves.
      The trunks are rough enough to climb. Sweet, and it quenches a little thirst.
    sketch: meadow
    trigger: 43
    triggerId: 
  - id: boiled_water
    title: Boiled Water
    category: 0
    text: Pond water looks clean but it is not. Heated over the fire until it bubbles,
      it sits easy in the stomach. Always boil before drinking.
    sketch: water
    trigger: 44
    triggerId: 
  - id: stomach_sick
    title: Sick
    category: 0
    text: My stomach cramps and I am weak and thirsty. Bad water or raw meat. Rest,
      drink boiled water, and it will pass.
    sketch: rocks
    trigger: 45
    triggerId: 
